Er, preferably nothing at all.  There's no good reason to be overriding
gcc's default optimization here; your package should be targetting the same
instruction set as the rest of the Debian architecture, whatever that
happens to be at the time.

At the moment, I believe -mcpu=ev5 happens to be the correct option.

